# Line endings are pinned to LF for everything the toolchain reads.
#
# This is not style. On Windows, git converts to CRLF on checkout by default, so
# a run's isolated worktree gets CRLF sources while the developer's tree has LF —
# and `gofmt -l` reports every converted file as needing a rewrite. The gate then
# refuses every run with a red format check over a tree nobody edited, and the
# fleet stalls with a message that describes the wrong problem entirely.
*.go      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
